# Injected into the containers via env_file, by every compose file in http/ and
# https/. Dev defaults that work out of the box; this file is tracked
# deliberately, the same way ignis tracks its docker.env, so a fresh clone runs
# without editing anything.
#
# One copy, shared by both environments, because the value does not depend on
# the transport in front of the service.

# CORS: origins allowed to call this API from a browser page. Comma-separated,
# no trailing slash.
#
# This is not an access control. A browser enforces it on behalf of a page it
# loaded; a server-to-server caller such as the EnerPlanET backend sends no
# Origin header and ignores the response headers entirely. What restricts who
# can reach the service is the network it is published on.
#
# buem-gateway's own middleware reads this list. In https/ the reverse proxy
# also derives its preflight matcher from it at container start.
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://localhost:3000,http://127.0.0.1:8000,https://enerplanet.github.io
